System boundary: the Health API's unauthenticated GET /health endpoint.
Actor: any client. When a client sends a GET /health request with no request
body, the Health API shall return HTTP status 200, Content-Type
application/json with no parameters, and exactly the byte sequence
{"status":"ok"} as the response body. Measure the maximum 100 ms response
time from receipt of the complete request headers at the Health API process
boundary to emission of the final response byte at that same boundary. The
maximum is P100: every request must meet it. A health request is concurrent
from complete-header receipt until final-byte emission; this requirement
applies while no more than 50 such requests are in flight at the process
boundary. Non-GET requests, request bodies, error responses, and behavior
above 50 concurrent requests are covered by separate requirements.
